# Opt-in rustls 0.23.46 ClientHello shaping for vendor egress.
# The default config and ordering stay upstream-compatible. The hook validates
# wire-only additions; retains dynamic HRR/resumption extensions; encodes padding
# before PSK binders; tracks sent extensions; and rejects unsupported EtM replies.
# Public wire/handshake tests cover ordering, retries, padding, and resumption.
# Upstream plan: propose a reviewed generic ClientHello customization interface;
# rebase this patch for each rustls security release until that interface exists.
# Invalid shapes return Error::General before the handshake is sent.

